WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.290
The Giant's Causeway: some
40,000 basalt columns,

2
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:09.430
formed by volcanic activity
50 to 60 million years ago.

3
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.070
No one built them.

4
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.910
Now cross to England's
Lake District: open fells,

5
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.790
stone walls, and Herdwick
sheep grazing the common land.

6
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.370
Stand on a hillside like this,
with no buildings in sight,

7
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.190
and it looks wild.

8
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.470
But is it natural?

9
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.250
Or did people make it what it is?

10
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.150
In this mission, you'll trace a Lake
District valley as a human system,

11
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.470
from inputs to outputs.

12
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.390
Then you'll put the idea
of wilderness to the test,

13
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.110
from the fells to
Scotland's map of wild land.

14
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.030
Your mission: decide whether a
wild-looking landscape is natural,

15
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.600
or made by people.
